WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
Today's news is all about positivity.

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.780 line:15%
And what better way to focus on the positive than an entire

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.510 line:15%
newspaper dedicated to good news.

4
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.120 line:15%
Yeah, that's right.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.570 line:15%
This is The Happy News.

6
00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:17.920 line:15%
A British publication dedicated to only good news

7
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.020 line:15%
in the world, look how great this is.

8
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.450 line:15%
I mean, come on.

9
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.540 line:15%
I grew up with pages of magazines lining my walls

10
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.840
like wallpaper.

11
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.460
In fact, I actually make a zine.

12
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:33.053
It's true, I'm not just all words, I'm action.

13
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.920
So the news team that I work with,

14
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.520
they brought me this paper.

15
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.750
They put it to my attention because they know

16
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.200
that I'm obsessed with good news.

17
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.010
And now I'm obsessed with the woman who makes this.

18
00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.210
I'm kinda convinced she's my British soul sister

19
00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.520
and here to talk about her newspaper, The Happy News,

20
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.708
please welcome Emily Coxhead.

21
00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:56.541
(audience applauding)
Hi.

22
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.610
I think that will be the best introduction I've ever had.

23
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.620
Oh my God, well, I could have gotten a lot more psycho

24
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.110
overboard, I kind of had to tame down because I've like,

25
00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.860
I feel like we've been separated at birth, I really do.

26
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.910
I mean, you love happy news, I love happy news.

27
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:18.320
You have an amazing design blog with your boyfriend

28
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.740
that I totally love.

29
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.740
I was scouring the Instagram account and I just love

30
00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.670
what you're putting out into the world.

31
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.730
That's something I really subscribe to, I did it.

32
00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.090
I said it, that's right.

33
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:35.610
Can I ask you since I'm just meeting my soul sister

34
00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:39.400
for the first time, why did you create The Happy News?

35
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.233
I don't know.

36
00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.290 line:15%
I was sort of struggling with my own mental health

37
00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.430 line:15%
and I think the two things that were impacting it

38
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.590 line:15%
the most were social media and the news.

39
00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.810
And I sort of began to realize that it was having that same

40
00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.020
effect on far more people than I'd realized.

41
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.870
So when I started looking for the good

42
00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.420
and then sharing the good things,

43
00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.500 line:15%
I then noticed the positive effect it was having

44
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.190 line:15%
on both me and other people.

45
00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.810 line:15%
And now, I think it's just needed.

46
00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.020 line:15%
I think we just need to...

47
00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.580 line:15%
In a world that's full of overwhelm I think we should

48
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.810 line:15%
be hearing about the kind people, you know?

49
00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.770
The amazing things that happen in the world,

50
00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.220
we just don't hear about.

51
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.500
Do you have any tips for digesting the realities

52
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.600
of the world because we can't ignore them,

53
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.353
what do you do?

54
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.110 line:15%
I think notice the impact it's having on you for a start.

55
00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.130 line:15%
I think be mindful about how you're feeling when you read

56
00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.740 line:15%
a newspaper, when you've been scrolling through social media

57
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.510 line:15%
or any of those things.

58
00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.950
I think you've got to look hard for the good things

59
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.420
but they are there.

60
00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.620
Yeah you've just got to look a little bit harder

61
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.890
than what's on the surface.

62
00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:50.740
I Get on a feeder and it doesn't always make me

63
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.940
the happiest person.

64
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.150
I feel really informed and up to the minute but it's true.

65
00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:01.110
It depletes my battery, my energy, my hope.

66
00:03:02.555 --> 00:03:04.460
Yeah, that's the biggest thing

67
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.380
and that's what I've said from the beginning

68
00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:09.380
of the newspaper, I want to give people hope

69
00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.803
and I want people to realize that there are good things.

70
00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.970
It's a really weird balance because obviously

71
00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:18.860
whenever I've done any sort of press things,

72
00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.570
you sort of get the people who are like, so naive

73
00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.280
or you're sticking your head in the sand.

74
00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.020
And I never want to try and cover up the bad

75
00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.770
and pretend that the world is just full of sunshine

76
00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.273
and rainbows because it isn't.

77
00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.620
And I always try to acknowledge that.

78
00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.580
What you're doing with your paper is you're giving

79
00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.040
your lens of the world and we need this.

80
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.020
Emily, keep it up.

81
00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.730 line:15%
Let's stay the soul sisters that we are.

82
00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:46.690 line:15%
If I may interject myself into your life that way.

83
00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.730
See, I told you it was going to get creepy.

84
00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.100
Emily, thank you so much.

85
00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.520
I'm so happy to know you.

86
00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.000 line:15%
Thank you news crew for bringing us together.

87
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.723 line:15%
Can we please hang out again?

88
00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.840
Definitely, thank you so much for having me.

89
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.293
I'm with you, let's keep up the good fight.

90
00:04:02.293 --> 00:04:03.500
(audience applauding)

91
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.240
All right, moving on.

92
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.880
Okay, our next story,

93
